{% extends 'demos/live_demo.html.twig' %}

{% block demo_container %}

    <div class="LivePaginationStage max-w-[1220px] mx-auto mb-12">
        <twig:Browser
            class="LivePaginationBrowser shadow-blur shadow-blur--rainbow w-full"
            :syncUrl="true"
            :showOrigin="false"
            :showQuery="false"
        >
            <twig:LivePagination :page="page" paginationRoute="app_demo_live_component_pagination" />
        </twig:Browser>

        <div class="LivePaginationNotes" aria-label="Live pagination notes">
            <twig:InfoCard
                id="live-pagination-note-url"
                title="The page lives in the URL"
                number="1"
                target=".LivePaginationBrowser .browser_url-path"
                class="LivePaginationNote LivePaginationNote--url"
            >
                <p>Follow a pagination link and both the real route and this browser address update.</p>
            </twig:InfoCard>

            <twig:InfoCard
                id="live-pagination-note-filters"
                title="Filters reset the page"
                number="2"
                target=".LivePaginationBrowser .filters"
                class="LivePaginationNote LivePaginationNote--filters"
            >
                <p>Changing any filter returns the pagination to page 1 before rendering the new result set.</p>
            </twig:InfoCard>

            <twig:InfoCard
                id="live-pagination-note-navigation"
                title="Every control remains a link"
                number="3"
                target=".LivePaginationBrowser .nav"
                class="LivePaginationNote LivePaginationNote--navigation"
            >
                <p>Previous, numbered and next controls keep real URLs. LiveComponent only enhances them.</p>
            </twig:InfoCard>
        </div>
    </div>

    <section class="LivePaginationExplanation py-12" style="padding-top: 6rem;">
        <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
            <twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow
                filename="src/Controller/Demo/LiveDemoController.php"
                :lineStart="97"
                :lineEnd="112"
                reversed
                sticky
            >
## Route the page number

The route makes the page number part of the URL and constrains it to positive
integers. The controller passes its initial value to the LiveComponent.

Open, refresh, or share `/pagination/12`: the component starts on page 12 even
before JavaScript runs.
            </twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="LivePaginationExplanation py-12">
        <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
            <twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow
                filename="src/Twig/Components/LivePagination.php"
                :lineStart="31"
                :lineEnd="64"
                sticky
            >
## Build the paginator

`UrlMapping(mapPath: true)` keeps the writable page property in the route path.
`ComponentWithPaginationTrait` provides the current pagination and its navigation
actions.

During a Live request, `color` and `pattern` live in the component payload rather
than Symfony's current query string. Passing them to `queryParameters()` keeps
every generated `href` equivalent to the filtered view, including without
JavaScript.

After a filter changes, `resetPage()` prevents the previous page from pointing
beyond the new result set.
            </twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="LivePaginationExplanation py-12">
        <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
            <twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow filename="templates/components/LivePagination/Pagination.html.twig" reversed sticky>
## Render real links

`ux_pagination()` renders accessible controls with real URLs. The demo supplies
only its page-grouping theme and the LiveComponent link attributes.

LiveComponent enhances navigation without replacing the links, so they still work
without JavaScript. Build a complete setup in the [Pagination
Studio]({{ path('app_demo_live_component_pagination_studio') }}).
            </twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow>
        </div>
    </section>

{% endblock %}
